  (b) bad classes avoiding the factor 111 (no low rescue point with a 2-step partner):
   L    |Bad_L|         no-111 part     fraction     growth (log2 ratio per step, window 10)
    8              19                1   5.26e-02     
   12             226                2   8.85e-03     
   16            2114                3   1.42e-03     
   20           27328                9   3.29e-04     0.3170
   24          286581               15   5.23e-05     0.2322
   30        12771274               59   4.62e-06     0.2713
   40      6402835000              409   6.39e-08     0.2793
   60  2216134944775156            40425   1.82e-11     0.3430
   80                          3316986      -         0.3640
  100                        285555273      -         0.2946
   => bad words with no factor 111 at all grow like 2^(0.3 L): on them no F-rescue (low up-image = 3 mod 4 with a
      2-step partner) ever exists; they contain the 2-adic cycle (110)^inf = -5 -> -7 -> -10.  The construction
      needs its B-rescue (partner not 2-step) only when also A is blocked, which forces n = -5 mod 2^9 (note, lemma C6).

